            "description": "Records how a SUBMITTED order was paid: creates and immediately submits a Payment Entry against the Sales Invoice in one step — this is what posts the GL entries and flips the invoice's status to 'Paid'. Must be called AFTER /submit (ERPNext rejects a Payment Entry referencing a draft invoice with 'Sales Invoice X must be submitted').\n\npayment_method: cash | mpesa — resolved (case/punctuation-insensitively) against the tenant's configured Mode of Payment; the request fails clearly listing the available modes if none match\namount_tendered: amount the customer physically handed over; change_due in the response = max(0, amount_tendered - grand_total) (amount applied to the invoice is capped at grand_total)\ntransaction_ref: M-Pesa receipt number (omit/null for cash); also doubles as an idempotency key — replaying the same request with the same ref returns the already-recorded Payment Entry instead of creating a duplicate (this is also how the Kafka PaymentEvent consumer stays idempotent on redelivery)"
